  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1231 AM MDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nUpper ridge amplifies over the area on Friday, with a trend\ntoward hotter and drier conditions developing. Will still be\nenough moisture around for isolated to scattered\nafternoon/evening showers/storms, though overall Fri may end up\nbeing the driest day we've seen over the past week. Upper ridge\nthen slips eastward on Sat, with increasing swly flow across srn\nCO. Pattern will keep hot temperatures going another day, with a\nfew 100f readings returning to the plains. Mid level moisture\nalso increases, with scattered to numerous shower/storms over \nthe mountains Sat afternoon, especially back toward the \nContinental Divide, while the plains see isolated activity \nmoving off the mountains late in the day. Upper trough moves\nthrough the nrn Rockies into the nrn plains on Sun, with sw \nflow across CO bringing back deepening moisture, especially \nalong the Continental Divide. Expect widespread showers/storms \nover the mountains Sun, with again less activity over the \nplains. Cold front then pushes through late Sun into Mon, while \nsw flow aloft persists ahead of Pacific Coast upper trough.\nExpect an upturn in convection all areas as a result, with\nrenewed low level moisture on the plains and upper level jet\noverhead. After peaking on Sat, max temps will drift downward \nSun-Tue, as cooler air filters into the region.",
